                "word": "géoéconomie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8dacb4a7-e070-3055-b411-e2b3e3b4f1ce",
                        "entry_id": "b4a3e7ea-2b36-355b-92cb-3bbf9b134899",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Branche des relations internationales, au croisement des sciences économiques et de la géopolitique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "460e4da6-bfca-422d-8cfa-b3025fc493a1",
                                "sense_id": "8dacb4a7-e070-3055-b411-e2b3e3b4f1ce",
                                "text": "Les États, même les plus libéraux, comme l’explique la géoéconomie, accordent soit des aides à l’exportation, soit, de manière plus détournée, des subventions ou des compensations au producteur, de manière à ce qu’ils puissent proposer des prix très attractifs sur les marchés étrangers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "65ac5be6-e213-40f5-ad08-76d8d0674fc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4a3e7ea-2b36-355b-92cb-3bbf9b134899",
                        "source_sense_id": "8dacb4a7-e070-3055-b411-e2b3e3b4f1ce",
                        "target_lang_word": "geoeconomics",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "geoeconomics",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ceb3b780-ab1f-39bc-871e-fd814f6b0383",
                                        "entry_id": "30ec9cc1-8642-372d-8046-a5e0154e7e31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The study of the spatial, temporal, and political aspects of economies and resources in relation to the balance of power between nation-states or trade blocs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16e3e7c8-7aba-4a57-a94c-0101095f5556",
                                                "sense_id": "ceb3b780-ab1f-39bc-871e-fd814f6b0383",
                                                "text": "Hidden behind thickets of acronyms and gorse bushes of detail, a new great game is under way across the globe. Some call it geoeconomics, but it's geopolitics too. The current power play consists of an extraordinary range of countries simultaneously sitting down to negotiate big free trade and investment agreements."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3b068b8-7320-44ba-9355-1afd6f4e5e3e",
                                                "sense_id": "ceb3b780-ab1f-39bc-871e-fd814f6b0383",
                                                "text": "‘Country risk’ is essentially about assessing the economic prospects of a nation holistically, within the broader legal and geopolitical soil without which institutional investors cannot grow their assets. The government of Qatar is now paying an incommensurate price for having thought it could defy forever the laws of geoeconomic gravity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00e8d489-4b22-4acf-a190-f7d9763e552e",
                                                "sense_id": "ceb3b780-ab1f-39bc-871e-fd814f6b0383",
                                                "text": "So universities like John Hopkins, Dartmouth, Kiel and Stanford are looking to expand their “geoeconomics” programmes (with the latter using machine learning for that end), along with entities such as the IMF, the Milken Institute and Atlantic Council."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "908ac9d8-cf44-4141-a8c7-c8e85cc04258",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4a3e7ea-2b36-355b-92cb-3bbf9b134899",
                        "source_sense_id": "8dacb4a7-e070-3055-b411-e2b3e3b4f1ce",
